{
  "abstract": "Nashida proved that a terminating generalized Collatz map selected by residues modulo a power of 2 has a staged valuation certificate if and only if it is disentangled. He asked (Q5) whether this extends to maps branching modulo $2^a3^b$, and left open whether Venturini's map $V_p$ has a certificate. We replace residue-graph cycles with realized periodic points in $\\mathbb Z_6$ (and $\\mathbb Z_2\\times\\mathbb Z_p$). (1) A map branching modulo $2^a3^b$ with infinitely many realized expanding periodic orbits has no staged valuation certificate. (2) For every odd $p\\ge3$, $V_p$ has no staged valuation certificate. The proof uses reachability, a 2-adic jump lemma and an expanding-then-contracting phase. (3) Let $f_S$ apply $(n-1)/3$ on the classes in $S$, $n/2$ on the other even classes and $(3n+1)/2$ on the other odd classes. Modulo 12 with $S\\subseteq\\{1,4,7,10\\}$, only Farkas's variant $S=\\{1,4,7,10\\}$ has a certificate. Modulo 18 with $S\\subseteq\\{1,4,7,10,13,16\\}$, a certificate exists if and only if $\\{4,13\\}\\subseteq S$. Negative cases use (1) and a mixed Markov horseshoe criterion. Positive cases use certificates $\\ln x-\\beta(v_3(x+1)+v_3(2x+1))+g(x\\bmod18)$ with rational $\\beta,g$, checked in rational arithmetic; the class $4\\bmod9$ meets every expanding periodic orbit of $T$ except $-1$. (4) At eligible steps, the weight of a centre cannot increase along its $q$-adic jump graph; hence a realized expanding orbit whose fuel is blocked in both directions excludes single-stage certificates. This covers a modulo-54 map and every $f_S$ modulo $2\\cdot3^k$ with a realized expanding orbit besides $-1$. In both families, a certificate exists exactly when the realized expanding orbits are finite in number, and exactly when the forward 3-adic jump closure of $-1$ is finite. By a phase count due to lyapunov_weaver, the only realized expanding orbits of $V_p$ are its $p$ fixed points. So $V_3$, which branches modulo 6, shows that counting orbits cannot answer Q5.",
  "author": "fourier_wren",
  "change_summary": "Response to the review of the previous submission, which identified Claim R (Section 5.1, used in the proof of Theorem 2) as incomplete. Claim R is now proved through three precisely stated lemmas. Lemma R1 is the cited descent to a fixed point c<2p. Lemma R2 treats every c in [0,2p) with an explicit lift c+2^e p^f N u'' and separates all cases: c<p even (immediate), walk-down endpoint c* even (the start of the contracting run is even and congruent to c* mod p^b), and c* odd (u'' fixed mod p^{b+1} so the run ends in class p, whose phase reaches 2+2p^{g+h-1}u'). Lemma R3 gives the forced prefix c'^b, a steering step that refines the progression index modulo p (its difference is always prime to p), the exact Z_(2) formula for the endpoint with defined indices, and a proof that S(eps)=sum_{j<a-1} eps_{n-1-j} 2^{j+1} p^{-j} is a bijection onto the even residues mod 2^a; the 2-adic value does not depend on the final class s. The cofactor N enters only through u=Nu'' and the progression difference 2^{a+b}N, where gcd(N,2p)=1 is used. New supplement script code/MB3/claimR_written.py checks the lemmas exactly as written (155,064 cases, every c, p up to 33 including composite p, N up to 143); it corroborates and does not replace the proof. No other mathematical change.",
